{
  "declined": "none",
  "criteria": [
    {
      "id": "taskAchievement",
      "score": 8.0,
      "reason": "述題清楚，涵蓋主要趨勢與比較，例如寫出“coal...providing 55%”和“solar power...from 5% to 20%”，並提供了整體概述“natural gas had replaced coal as the largest source”。"
    },
    {
      "id": "coherence",
      "score": 8.0,
      "reason": "結構清晰，段落分明且順序合理（概述、詳細比較、補充觀察），例如開頭句“The table compares the proportion...”引導全文。"
    },
    {
      "id": "lexical",
      "score": 8.0,
      "reason": "用詞準確且多樣，如“relied less on coal”、“the most dramatic change”、“energy mix”，詞彙恰當且自然。"
    },
    {
      "id": "grammarRange",
      "score": 8.0,
      "reason": "句型與時態使用正確，包含比較結構與被動/完成式表達，句子如“In 2010, coal was by far the most important source”文法正確。"
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "quote": "It is worth noting that the three sources together made up 90% of electricity in 2010 and 95% in 2020, which suggests that the remaining sources, such as wind or nuclear power, became slightly less important.",
      "type": "task",
      "why": "這句中數字與題目資料矛盾：題目三者在2010合計應為90% (55+30+5)=90，但在2020應為95% (35+40+20)=95，句子結論推論“remaining sources...became slightly less important”沒有資料支持，因為三者合計增加只表示份額轉移，不代表其他來源絕對值下降。",
      "suggestion": "Rewrite to avoid implying absolute decline: \"The three sources together accounted for 90% of electricity in 2010 and 95% in 2020, indicating that these three grew as a share of the total generation.\""
    },
    {
      "quote": "By 2020, natural gas had replaced coal as the largest source of electricity.",
      "type": "grammar",
      "why": "時態與語氣雖可接受，但使用過去完成時（had replaced）在兩個時間點的對比中稍顯多餘，簡單過去時更直接且常見。",
      "suggestion": "Use simple past: \"By 2020, natural gas replaced coal as the largest source of electricity.\""
    },
    {
      "quote": "The most dramatic change was seen in solar power, which quadrupled from 5% to 20% and became a significant part of the energy mix.",
      "type": "word-choice",
      "why": "這句很好，但“quadrupled”後接百分比時讀者可能會混淆絕對與相對變化；可稍微明確說明為百分點或倍數。",
      "suggestion": "Clarify: \"solar power increased from 5% to 20% (a fourfold rise).\""
    }
  ],
  "more": [
    {
      "quote": "the country relied less on coal over the decade",
      "type": "grammar",
      "why": "表達正確但可更精確，例如指出減少的幅度以便更具體。",
      "suggestion": "\"the country relied less on coal over the decade, with its share falling by 20 percentage points.\""
    },
    {
      "quote": "Natural gas accounted for 30%, whereas solar power produced only 5%.",
      "type": "punctuation",
      "why": "句內逗號使用正常，但可改為分句或使用連接詞讓句子更流暢。",
      "suggestion": "\"Natural gas accounted for 30%, while solar power produced only 5%.\""
    },
    {
      "quote": "Ten years later, the figure for coal had dropped by 20 percentage points to 35%.",
      "type": "verb",
      "why": "此處同樣使用過去完成時（had dropped）非必要，簡單過去更符合時間線敘述。",
      "suggestion": "\"Ten years later, the figure for coal dropped by 20 percentage points to 35%.\""
    },
    {
      "quote": "the shares of natural gas and especially solar power rose.",
      "type": "cohesion",
      "why": "短語中使用\"especially\"強調solar，但句子略為簡短，建議稍擴充以更清楚說明程度差異。",
      "suggestion": "\"the shares of natural gas and, especially, solar power rose significantly.\""
    },
    {
      "quote": "which suggests that the remaining sources, such as wind or nuclear power, became slightly less important.",
      "type": "cohesion",
      "why": "同一句包含推論，應避免超出給定數據的合理推斷（見主要問題），並可用更保守的語氣。",
      "suggestion": "\"which suggests that these three sources increased their share of total generation.\""
    }
  ],
  "strengths": [
    {
      "quote": "Overall, the country relied less on coal over the decade, while the shares of natural gas and especially solar power rose.",
      "why": "清楚提出總體趨勢，概述段寫得直接且涵蓋對比重點，符合Task 1要點。"
    },
    {
      "quote": "The most dramatic change was seen in solar power, which quadrupled from 5% to 20% and became a significant part of the energy mix.",
      "why": "善用強調語（\"most dramatic\"）和具體數據描述，讓讀者快速掌握主要變化。"
    }
  ],
  "summary": "你已經能夠清楚描述趨勢並正確使用數據來比較不同能源的變化。接下來注意避免做出超出表格資料的推論（例如其他能源“變得不重要”），並在時間對比句中以簡單過去時表述會更自然。繼續練習用更精確的描述（百分點與倍數分別標示）會讓文章更專業。"
}
